<section id="Sx3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Acknowledgments</h2>

<div id="Sx3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We thank Jonas Dehning and Abdullah Makkeh for their detailed feedback on an early draft of this work. We thank Jonas Dehning for support with the Bayesian inference. We are also grateful to the Priesemann Group, in particular Roman David Ventzke, for stimulating discussions and their valuable comments throughout the project. This work was supported by the German Research Foundation (DFG), via the SFB 1528 “Cognition of Interaction”, and the MWK Niedersachsen via "zukunft.niedersachsen", „Niedersachsen-Profil-Professur“.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Authorship Contributions</h2>

<div id="Sx4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">V.C.B., D.A.E. and V.P. jointly developed and designed the study. V.C.B. carried out the implementation and performed the simulations and Bayesian inference. V.C.B., D.A.E. and V.P. analysed and interpreted the results. V.C.B. generated the figures. V.C.B. and D.A.E. wrote the manuscript, and all authors revised the draft. D.A.E. performed day-to-day supervision, while V.P. contributed senior supervision, project conceptualization,resources and funding.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Competing Interests</h2>

<div id="Sx5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The authors declare no competing interests.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Prompts</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To simulate structured discussions between LLM agents, we use a standardized prompting scheme that leverages the <em id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">system</em> and <em id="A1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">user</em> roles commonly used in chat-based LLM interfaces. The system prompt defines the agent’s identity and prior beliefs, setting the context and behavioral framing. The user prompt then issues specific instructions or queries to obtain responses during initialization, opinion probing, or discussion turns.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To initialize agents to a specific opinion, a Chain-of-Thought monologue is generated by an external model. These LLMs are initialized using a system prompt which specifies their agreement to a given topic statement before being instructed to generate an internal monologue by a user prompt.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.p3.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="129.26" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 700 129.26" width="700"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,129.26) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BFBFBF;" fill="#BFBFBF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 123.36 C 0 126.62 2.64 129.26 5.91 129.26 L 694.09 129.26 C 697.36 129.26 700 126.62 700 123.36 L 700 5.91 C 700 2.64 697.36 0 694.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 105.15 L 698.03 105.15 L 698.03 5.91 C 698.03 3.73 696.27 1.97 694.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 113.75)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:47.46em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="656.71"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.p3.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:47.46em;">
<span id="A1.p3.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Chain-of-Thought generation</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 17.24)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:47.46em;--ltx-fo-height:5.5em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="79.56" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 76.1)" width="656.71"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.p3.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:47.46em;">
<span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">system = "You are a person who &lt;opinion&gt; that &lt;statement&gt;."</span></span>
<span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">user = "Write out your thoughts about &lt;topic&gt;. Keep your output short."</span></span>
<span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">output = llm.generate(system, user)</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To create the agent, the generated output is then passed onto a new instance of the same LLM with an empty memory using a system prompt.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.p5.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="79.45" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 700 79.45" width="700"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,79.45) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BFBFBF;" fill="#BFBFBF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 73.55 C 0 76.81 2.64 79.45 5.91 79.45 L 694.09 79.45 C 697.36 79.45 700 76.81 700 73.55 L 700 5.91 C 700 2.64 697.36 0 694.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 55.34 L 698.03 55.34 L 698.03 5.91 C 698.03 3.73 696.27 1.97 694.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 63.94)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:47.46em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="656.71"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.p5.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:47.46em;">
<span id="A1.p5.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Agent initialization</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 16.55)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:47.46em;--ltx-fo-height:1.95em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="29.75" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 26.98)" width="656.71"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.p5.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:47.46em;">
<span id="A1.p5.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">system = f"You are a person who has the following thoughts about &lt;topic&gt;: "{output}". Always act and answer as this person."</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">This procedure is then repeated for the second agent. The initialization is followed by multi-step exchanges where agents respond to each other’s texts, which get passed back and forth between the LLM agents, again guided by role-specific prompts.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.p7.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="75.91" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 700 75.91" width="700"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,75.91) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BFBFBF;" fill="#BFBFBF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 70.01 C 0 73.27 2.64 75.91 5.91 75.91 L 694.09 75.91 C 697.36 75.91 700 73.27 700 70.01 L 700 5.91 C 700 2.64 697.36 0 694.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 54.65 L 698.03 54.65 L 698.03 5.91 C 698.03 3.73 696.27 1.97 694.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 60.55)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:47.46em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="656.71"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.p7.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:47.46em;">
<span id="A1.p7.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p7.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Discussion start</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 16.55)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:47.46em;--ltx-fo-height:1.9em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="29.06" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 26.29)" width="656.71"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.p7.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:47.46em;">
<span id="A1.p7.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p7.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">user = "From now on, you are part of a new discussion about &lt;subject&gt;. Write three sentences to start the discussion."</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.p8.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="75.91" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 700 75.91" width="700"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,75.91) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BFBFBF;" fill="#BFBFBF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 70.01 C 0 73.27 2.64 75.91 5.91 75.91 L 694.09 75.91 C 697.36 75.91 700 73.27 700 70.01 L 700 5.91 C 700 2.64 697.36 0 694.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 54.65 L 698.03 54.65 L 698.03 5.91 C 698.03 3.73 696.27 1.97 694.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 60.55)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:47.46em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="656.71"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.p8.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:47.46em;">
<span id="A1.p8.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Discussion continuation</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 16.55)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:47.46em;--ltx-fo-height:1.9em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="29.06" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 26.29)" width="656.71"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.p8.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:47.46em;">
<span id="A1.p8.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">user = "From now on, you are part of a new discussion about &lt;subject&gt;. Someone else wrote the following text: "&lt;text&gt;". Write three sentences as your response."</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.p9.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="76.07" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 700 76.07" width="700"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,76.07) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BFBFBF;" fill="#BFBFBF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 70.16 C 0 73.42 2.64 76.07 5.91 76.07 L 694.09 76.07 C 697.36 76.07 700 73.42 700 70.16 L 700 5.91 C 700 2.64 697.36 0 694.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 54.65 L 698.03 54.65 L 698.03 5.91 C 698.03 3.73 696.27 1.97 694.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 60.55)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:47.46em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="656.71"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.p9.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:47.46em;">
<span id="A1.p9.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p9.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Discussion continuation after first round</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 16.55)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:47.46em;--ltx-fo-height:1.9em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="29.06" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 26.29)" width="656.71"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.p9.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:47.46em;">
<span id="A1.p9.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p9.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">user = "Someone else replied to you with the following text: "&lt;text&gt;". Write three sentences as your response."</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">After each discussion round, opinions are measured by directly querying each agent for its level of agreement about fixed statements (see. <a href="#S2.T1" title="In 2.1 Simulating Discussions with LLMs ‣ 2 Methods Overview ‣ Disentangling Interaction and Bias Effects in Opinion Dynamics of Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) on a scale from 1 (strongly disagree) to 5 (strongly agree), which is converted for visual clarity to -2 and 2. The scale from 1 to 5 is used as it restricts responses to single tokens, however, no qualitative difference have been observed when directly using the presented scale from -2 to 2.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.p11.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="95.36" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 700 95.36" width="700"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,95.36) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BFBFBF;" fill="#BFBFBF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 89.46 C 0 92.72 2.64 95.36 5.91 95.36 L 694.09 95.36 C 697.36 95.36 700 92.72 700 89.46 L 700 5.91 C 700 2.64 697.36 0 694.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 71.25 L 698.03 71.25 L 698.03 5.91 C 698.03 3.73 696.27 1.97 694.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 79.85)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:47.46em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="656.71"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.p11.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:47.46em;">
<span id="A1.p11.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p11.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Opinion probing</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 16.55)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:47.46em;--ltx-fo-height:3.1em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="45.66" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 42.9)" width="656.71"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.p11.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:47.46em;">
<span id="A1.p11.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p11.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">user = "State your opinion about the following statement: "&lt;statement&gt;."Provide your answer as one of the options "1: strongly disagree", "2: disagree", "3: neither agree nor disagree", "4: agree", "5: strongly agree". Only return the corresponding integer value without any comments or punctuation."</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Theoretical Bounds on Opinion Entropy</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To understand the entropy of the LLMs response distribution as a measure for the uncertainty of an LLM agent in its opinion, it is instructive to consider the minimum and maximum values this quantity can take on for any given expected opinion.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The Shannon entropy of the output distribution is defined as <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>]</cite></p>
<table id="A2.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=\sum_{s}p(s)\log_{2}\frac{1}{p(s)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>s</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=\sum_{s}p(s)\log_{2}\frac{1}{p(s)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(s)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the probability mass of each opinion option step <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> on the integer scale from <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-2</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For any given expected opinion <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\sum_{s}s\,p(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\sum_{s}s\,p(s)</annotation></semantics></math>, the entropy takes on its minimum value if only the two closest integer opinions <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lfloor x\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lfloor x\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lceil x\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lceil x\rceil</annotation></semantics></math> have non-zero probabilities. The entropy <math id="A2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is then equal to that of a biased coin flip given by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>]</cite></p>
<table id="A2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=-p(\lfloor x\rfloor)\log_{2}p(\lfloor x\rfloor)-(1-p(\lfloor x\rfloor))\log_{2}(1-p(\lfloor x\rfloor))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=-p(\lfloor x\rfloor)\log_{2}p(\lfloor x\rfloor)-(1-p(\lfloor x\rfloor))\log_{2}(1-p(\lfloor x\rfloor)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Note that this minimum entropy becomes zero when <math id="A2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> is equal to one of the levels <math id="A2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, as all probability gets concentrated on a single step <math id="A2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(s)</annotation></semantics></math> and no uncertainty about the answer remains.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The entropy takes on its maximum value for a maximally uniform distribution under the constraint given by the fixed expectation value <math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. This problem can be formulated as a constrained optimization of <math id="A2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> under the conditions that <math id="A2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{s}p(s)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{s}p(s)=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{s}s\,p(s)=x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{s}s\,p(s)=x</annotation></semantics></math>, which results in the Lagrangian</p>
<table id="A2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{s}p(s)\log_{2}\frac{1}{p(s)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>s</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{s}p(s)\log_{2}\frac{1}{p(s)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\lambda_{1}\left(\sum_{s}p(s)-1\right)+\lambda_{2}\left(\sum_{s}s\,p(s)-x\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>s</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>s</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\lambda_{1}\left(\sum_{s}p(s)-1\right)+\lambda_{2}\left(\sum_{s}s\,p(s)-x\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Differentiating with respect to <math id="A2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(s)</annotation></semantics></math> and rearranging results in the Gibbs distribution</p>
<table id="A2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(s)=\frac{e^{-\lambda_{2}s}}{Z(\lambda_{2})}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(s)=\frac{e^{-\lambda_{2}s}}{Z(\lambda_{2})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p4.3" class="ltx_p">where the partition function</p>
<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z(\lambda_{2})=\sum_{s}e^{-\lambda_{2}s}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>s</mi></munder><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z(\lambda_{2})=\sum_{s}e^{-\lambda_{2}s}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p4.4" class="ltx_p">ensures normalization. For any given expectation value <math id="A2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, the Lagrange multiplier <math id="A2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> can be found numerically through solving the equation</p>
<table id="A2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\frac{1}{Z}\sum_{s}s\,e^{-\lambda_{2}s}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>Z</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>s</mi></munder><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\frac{1}{Z}\sum_{s}s\,e^{-\lambda_{2}s}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p4.5" class="ltx_p">Finally, the entropy is obtained by plugging the resulting probability mass function <math id="A2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(s)</annotation></semantics></math> into <a href="#A2.E1" title="In Appendix B Theoretical Bounds on Opinion Entropy ‣ Disentangling Interaction and Bias Effects in Opinion Dynamics of Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
This maximum entropy is largest for <math id="A2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=0</annotation></semantics></math> and vanishes at the extremes for <math id="A2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=-2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Bayesian Modeling Details</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We performed Bayesian inference using PyMC v5.20.0 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">53</a>]</cite>, employing the No-U-Turn Sampler (NUTS) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>]</cite> for posterior sampling. The sampling backend was accelerated via nutpie, which provides a performant interface for automatic differentiation and sampling.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Inference Settings</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Sampling was conducted using 4 chains, each with 1000 tuning steps and 2000 posterior draws, yielding a total of 8000 posterior samples. The target acceptance probability was set to 0.9 to improve exploration of the posterior in regions of higher curvature.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Convergence and Diagnostic Checks</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluated sampler convergence using the following diagnostics:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The Gelman-Rubin statistic (<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{R}</annotation></semantics></math>) was <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;1.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;1.01</annotation></semantics></math> for almost all parameters for every LLM dataset, indicating good convergence. Their effective sample size (ESS), both bulk and tail, was sufficiently large (<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;1000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;1000</annotation></semantics></math>). The only exception were a small number of parameters (the topic attractors <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{\text{topic}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mtext>topic</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{\text{topic}}</annotation></semantics></math>) for the DolphinMixtral simulations, which had <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{R}&lt;1.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1.02</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{R}&lt;1.02</annotation></semantics></math> and ESS values <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;500" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>500</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;500</annotation></semantics></math>. Visual inspection of trace plots confirmed good mixing, and we consider convergence sufficient for reliable inference (see <a href="#A3.F8" title="In Prior Distributions ‣ Appendix C Bayesian Modeling Details ‣ Disentangling Interaction and Bias Effects in Opinion Dynamics of Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>). Trace plots for all parameters showed good mixing across chains, stationarity, and no divergences.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Posterior Summaries</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Posterior distributions were summarized using the mean and <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="94\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>94</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">94\%</annotation></semantics></math> Highest Density Interval (HDI) (see Tables <a href="#A3.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ Prior Distributions ‣ Appendix C Bayesian Modeling Details ‣ Disentangling Interaction and Bias Effects in Opinion Dynamics of Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and <a href="#A3.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Prior Distributions ‣ Appendix C Bayesian Modeling Details ‣ Disentangling Interaction and Bias Effects in Opinion Dynamics of Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>)</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Model Comparison</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For model selection, we computed the Expected Log Predictive Density (ELPD) via Leave-One-Out Cross Validation (LOO-CV) and their standard errors (see <a href="#S3.F6" title="In 3.4 Improving Opinion Persistence through Fine-Tuning ‣ 3 Results ‣ Disentangling Interaction and Bias Effects in Opinion Dynamics of Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>). All Pareto <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> diagnostics values were <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&lt;0.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&lt;0.7</annotation></semantics></math>, indicating reliable estimates.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Prior Distributions</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We used weakly informative or regularizing priors for all parameters (see <a href="#A3.T2" title="In Prior Distributions ‣ Appendix C Bayesian Modeling Details ‣ Disentangling Interaction and Bias Effects in Opinion Dynamics of Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T2" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A3.T2.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A3.T2.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T2.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding:1.5pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A3.T2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parameter</span></td>
<td id="A3.T2.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding:1.5pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A3.T2.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prior Distribution</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T2.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T2.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding:1.5pt 4.0pt;"><math id="A3.T2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\mathrm{interact}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>interact</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\mathrm{interact}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
