<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>The priors for <math id="A3.T2.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\mathrm{interact}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>interact</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\mathrm{interact}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.T2.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\text{topic}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mtext>topic</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\text{topic}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.T2.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\text{anchor}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mtext>anchor</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\text{anchor}}</annotation></semantics></math> were chosen weakly informative about the direction of influence with a standard normal distribution <math id="A3.T2.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(\mu=0,\sigma=1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(\mu=0,\sigma=1)</annotation></semantics></math> around mean <math id="A3.T2.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=0</annotation></semantics></math>, allowing for a broader range of values with <math id="A3.T2.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=1</annotation></semantics></math>. As the agreement bias does not correspond with a repulsive effect, we used a HalfNormal prior for <math id="A3.T2.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\text{agree}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mtext>agree</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\text{agree}}</annotation></semantics></math>, as well for parameters, that are not allowed to be positive. The values of the different attractors <math id="A3.T2.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> can lie within our opinion scale ranging from -2 to 2. Here, we used a weakly informative prior in the form of a uniform distribution <math id="A3.T2.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}(-2,2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}(-2,2)</annotation></semantics></math> across this range. We enlarged the half<span id="A3.T2.5" class="ltx_text">-</span>normal prior’s scale for <math id="A3.T2.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.T2.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=20</annotation></semantics></math> so that it reduces prior<span id="A3.T2.6" class="ltx_text">-</span>data conflict while still providing weak regularisation.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F8" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><img src="2509.06858v1/figures/appendix/trace_1.png" id="A3.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:219/332;" width="219" height="332" alt="Refer to caption"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><img src="2509.06858v1/figures/appendix/trace_2.png" id="A3.F8.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:219/330;" width="219" height="330" alt="Refer to caption"></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span>Traces of the parameter inference for DolphinMixtral. Topic biases are color coded for the “climate change” (blue), “AI safety” (orange) and “wealth distribution” (green) topics.</figcaption>
</figure>
